{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_NS to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; for (var i=0; i &lt; 4; i++) { if (SWI_meaning.substring(i,i+1) === '*' &amp;&amp; SWI_meaning.substring(i+1,5) !== Array(5-i).join('*')) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } }ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_esus_drivers_license_NS'</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><item repeat='5'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + A.V : A.V;</tag></item><item><one-of><item>star</item><item>asterisk</item></one-of><tag>V = V ? V + '*' : '*';</tag></item></one-of></item><one-of><item>nueve nueve nueve nueve nueve nueve<tag>V = V ? V + '999999' : '999999';</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DayOfMonth'/><tag>V = V ? V + DayOfMonth.V : DayOfMonth.V;</tag><ruleref uri='date.grxml#MonthOfYear'/><tag>V = V ? V + MonthOfYear.V : MonthOfYear.V;</tag><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of><item repeat='1-3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom Entity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The provided GRXML grammar defines a complex driver's license pattern that combines multiple alphanumeric, numeric, and special characters (\\\"*\\\", \\\"star\\\", \\\"asterisk\\\"), as well as structured dates. Such structure is best represented by a Custom Regular Expression (Regex) Entity in Microsoft Copilot Studio, as it consists of variable character combinations and numeric constraints with complex formatting rules.\n\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_NS\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_NS\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(?:[A-Za-z*]{5}(?:999999|\\d{2}\\d{2}\\d{2})\\d{1,3})$'\n    description: \\\"Matches a license pattern starting with five alphanumeric or '*' characters, followed by either '999999' or a structured 6-digit date format (DDMMYY), and ending with one to three digits.\\\"\n\nNote:\n- The regular expression above captures the described GRXML pattern. It includes:\n  - 5 repetitions of either letters (from alpha.grxml) or '*' (represented by \\\"star\\\"/\\\"asterisk\\\").\n  - Either the exact literal string '999999' or a date composed of DayOfMonth(2 digits), MonthOfYear(2 digits), and two additional numeric digits.\n  - Ends with 1-3 numeric digits, as defined in your GRXML file."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_NS_2 to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; for (var i=0; i &lt; 4; i++) { if (SWI_meaning.substring(i,i+1) === '*' &amp;&amp; SWI_meaning.substring(i+1,5) !== Array(5-i).join('*')) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } }ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_enus_drivers_license_NS'</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><item repeat='5'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + A.V : A.V;</tag></item><item><one-of><item>star</item><item>asterisk</item></one-of><tag>V = V ? V + '*' : '*';</tag></item></one-of></item><one-of><item>nine nine nine nine nine nine<tag>V = V ? V + '999999' : '999999';</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DayOfMonth'/><tag>V = V ? V + DayOfMonth.V : DayOfMonth.V;</tag><ruleref uri='date.grxml#MonthOfYear'/><tag>V = V ? V + MonthOfYear.V : MonthOfYear.V;</tag><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of><item repeat='1-3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The input GRXML grammar defines a structured and constrained pattern for recognizing driver's license numbers, composed of alphabetic characters (\"alpha\"), optional wildcard characters (\"asterisk/star\"), specific sequences (like \"nine nine nine nine nine nine\"), date components (day/month/digits) and additional digits. This structured alphanumeric pattern is best represented as a Custom Regex Entity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_NS_2\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_NS_2\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^[A-Za-z\\*]{5}((999999)|(\\d{2}\\d{2}\\d{2}))\\d{1,3}$'\n      validationMessage: \"Please enter a valid driver's license number format.\"\n      caseSensitive: false"}]}
