{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_PE(1) to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_enus_drivers_license_PE';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><one-of><item repeat='1-6'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><item><item repeat='4'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DayOfMonth'/><tag>V = V ? V + DayOfMonth.V : DayOfMonth.V;</tag><ruleref uri='date.grxml#MonthOfYear'/><tag>V = V ? V + MonthOfYear.V : MonthOfYear.V;</tag><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><one-of><item>one<tag>V = V ? V + '1' : '1';</tag></item><item>two<tag>V = V ? V + '2' : '2';</tag></item></one-of><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></one-of><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom Entity (RegexEntity)\nreason: \"The grammar describes a driver's license number entity, structured by digits and date components with specific numeric sequences. A prebuilt entity doesn't accurately represent this logic. Therefore, the best migration to Microsoft Copilot Studio is creating a RegexEntity to capture and validate license numbers matching the described pattern.\"\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_PE\n    state: Active\n    schemaName: DL_PE\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '(^\\d{1,6}$)|(^\\d{4}(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])(0[1-9]|1[0-2])\\d{2}[12]\\d$)'\n    status: Active\n\n# Explanation of Regex:\n# The above regex has two parts separated by an OR \"|\":\n#   (^\\\\d{1,6}$): Matches license numbers that are purely numeric, between 1 and 6 digits.\n#   (^\\\\d{4}(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])(0[1-9]|1[0-2])\\\\d{2}[12]\\\\d$): Matches a structured license number pattern\n#       - First 4 digits: fixed digits (\\\\d{4})\n#       - Next 2 digits (day of month): 01 to 31\n#       - Next 2 digits (month): 01 to 12\n#       - Next 2 digits: any two digits\n#       - Followed by one digit either 1 or 2 ([12])\n#       - Followed by one digit (\\\\d)\n\n# Notes:\n# - Digit placeholders (\\d) represent numeric values.\n# - \"date.grxml#DayOfMonth\" translated to day numeric range (01-31)\n# - \"date.grxml#MonthOfYear\" translated to month numeric range (01-12)"}]}
