{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file GlobalCommands to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#command'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) {var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^');disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow;for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) {if (command.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) {SWI_disallow=1;break;}}}if(command.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=command.dm_confirm_string};if(command.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=command.SWI_meaning};if(command.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=command.dm_confirmation_mode};dm_command=command.SWI_meaning;grammar_version='20131216';MEANING=SWI_meaning;</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='command' scope='public'><one-of><item><tag>SWI_meaning='operator'; dm_confirm_string='gl_cnf_operator'; dm_confirmation_mode='IF_NECESSARY'; </tag><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#OPERATOR'/></item></one-of></item><item><tag>SWI_meaning='main_menu';</tag><one-of><item><tag>dm_confirm_string='gl_cnf_mainMenu'; dm_confirmation_mode='IF_NECESSARY'; </tag><ruleref uri='#MAIN_MENU'/></item></one-of></item><item><tag>SWI_meaning='repeat';</tag><one-of><item><tag>dm_confirm_string=''; dm_confirmation_mode='NEVER'; </tag><ruleref uri='#REPEAT'/></item></one-of></item></one-of></rule><rule id='OPERATOR' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='./operator.grxml#OPERATOR'/></item></one-of></rule><rule id='MAIN_MENU' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='./main_menu.grxml#MAIN_MENU'/></item></one-of></rule><rule id='REPEAT' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='./repeat.grxml#REPEAT'/></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomListEntity\\nreason: The GRXML file defines a custom command grammar with custom meanings mapped to operator, main menu, and repeat functions. None of these correspond directly to prebuilt entities, making CustomListEntity appropriate for creating your own classifications and synonyms.\\ncopilot_studio_code: |\\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\\n    displayName: GlobalCommands\\n    state: Active\\n    status: Active\\n    schemaName: GlobalCommands\\n    entity:\\n      kind: ClosedListEntity\\n      items:\\n        - id: operator\\n          displayName: operator\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: main_menu\\n          displayName: main_menu\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: repeat\\n          displayName: repeat\\n          synonyms: []"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file hexadecimal to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' xml:lang='es-us' root='HEX'><rule id='HEX'><one-of><item>a<tag>V='A'</tag></item><item>b<tag>V='B'</tag></item><item>c<tag>V='C'</tag></item><item>d<tag>V='D'</tag></item><item>e<tag>V='E'</tag></item><item>f<tag>V='F'</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=DIGIT.V</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='DIGIT'><one-of><item>cero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>uno<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>dos<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>tres<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>cuatro<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>cinco<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>seis<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>siete<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>ocho<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nueve<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomListEntity\nreason: The provided GRXML represents a custom closed-list hexadecimal digit recognition grammar with letters (a-f) and number words in Spanish. It's not a prebuilt type since it combines specific entities not covered by built-in entities, so implementing a CustomListEntity is correct.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: hexadecimal\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: hexadecimal\n    entity:\n      kind: ClosedListEntity\n      items:\n        - id: A\n          displayName: A\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: B\n          displayName: B\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: C\n          displayName: C\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: D\n          displayName: D\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: E\n          displayName: E\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: F\n          displayName: F\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '0'\n          displayName: '0'\n          synonyms:\n            - cero\n        - id: '1'\n          displayName: '1'\n          synonyms:\n            - uno\n        - id: '2'\n          displayName: '2'\n          synonyms:\n            - dos\n        - id: '3'\n          displayName: '3'\n          synonyms:\n            - tres\n        - id: '4'\n          displayName: '4'\n          synonyms:\n            - cuatro\n        - id: '5'\n          displayName: '5'\n          synonyms:\n            - cinco\n        - id: '6'\n          displayName: '6'\n          synonyms:\n            - seis\n        - id: '7'\n          displayName: '7'\n          synonyms:\n            - siete\n        - id: '8'\n          displayName: '8'\n          synonyms:\n            - ocho\n        - id: '9'\n          displayName: '9'\n          synonyms:\n            - nueve"}]}
