nse number pattern), which begins consistently with two zeros (spoken as \\\"oh\\\" or \\\"zero\\\"), followed by seven digits spoken as words. Such structured numeric or alphanumeric sequences are best represented as Regular Expressions (RegexEntity) in Copilot Studio—not as closed synonyms list or prebuilt entities.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: license_LA\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: license_LA\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      pattern: '^(00)\\d{7}$'\n      regexFlags: None"}]}
