em>f<tag>V='F'</tag></item><item>g<tag>V='G'</tag></item><item>h<tag>V='H'</tag></item><item>i<tag>V='I'</tag></item><item>j<tag>V='J'</tag></item><item>k<tag>V='K'</tag></item><item>l<tag>V='L'</tag></item><item>m<tag>V='M'</tag></item><item>n<tag>V='N'</tag></item><item>o<tag>V='O'</tag></item><item>p<tag>V='P'</tag></item><item>q<tag>V='Q'</tag></item><item>r<tag>V='R'</tag></item><item>s<tag>V='S'</tag></item><item>t<tag>V='T'</tag></item><item>u<tag>V='U'</tag></item><item>v<tag>V='V'</tag></item><item>w<tag>V='W'</tag></item><item>x<tag>V='X'</tag></item><item>y<tag>V='Y'</tag></item><item>z<tag>V='Z'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The GRXML grammar describes a Wyoming vehicle license number format composed exclusively of numeric digits, either exactly 9 digits or exactly 10 digits. It uses digit-by-digit references and does not include letters or synonyms for distinct terms. This is best modeled as a regular expression (RegexEntity) rather than a closed list.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: license_WY\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: license_WY\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^\\d{9,10}$'\n      extractionMethod: Regex"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file main_menu to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#command'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (command.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(command.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=command.dm_confirm_string}; if(command.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=command.SWI_meaning}; if(command.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=command.dm_confirmation_mode}; dm_command=command.SWI_meaning; grammar_version='20131216'; MEANING=SWI_meaning;</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='command' scope='public'><one-of><item><tag>SWI_meaning='main_menu';</tag><one-of><item><tag>dm_confirm_string='gl_cnf_mainMenu'; dm_confirmation_mode='IF_NECESSARY';</tag><ruleref uri='#MAIN_MENU'/></item></one-of></item></one-of></rule><rule id='MAIN_MENU' scope='public'><one-of><item>main menu</item><item>start over</item><item weight='0.01'>go back to<item repeat='0-1'>the</item>main menu</item><item weight='0.01'>go to<item repeat='0-1'>the</item>main menu</item><item weight='0.01'>return to<item repeat='0-1'>the</item>main menu</item></one-of><item repeat='0-1'>please</item></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomListEntity\nreason: The GRXML grammar defines a command with one meaning (\"main_menu\") having several phrases as synonyms. This aligns with a ClosedListEntity, allowing various interchangeable user utterances mapped to one meaning. \ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: main_menu\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: main_menu\n    entity:\n      kind: ClosedListEntity\n      items:\n        - id: main_menu\n          displayName: main_menu\n          synonyms:\n            - start over\n            - go back to main menu\n            - go back to the main menu\n            - go to main menu\n            - go to the main menu\n            - return to main menu\n            - return to the main menu\n            - main menu please\n            - start over please\n            - go back to main menu please\n            - go back to the main menu please\n            - go to main menu please\n            - go to the main menu please\n            - return to main menu please\n            - return to the main menu please"}]}
