{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file meid to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' xml:lang='es-us' root='_meid'><rule id='_meid' scope='public'><item repeat='0-1'>@hes@</item><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#MEID_dec'/><tag>SWI_meaning=MEID_dec.V;if(SWI_meaning.length == 19){var mask=[0,2,4,6,8,1,3,5,7,9];var sum=0;var double_the_value=0;var i;var add;var allowed;for(i=SWI_meaning.length-1;i>=0;i--){add=parseInt(SWI_meaning[i],10);sum+=double_the_value?parseInt(mask[add],10):add;double_the_value=!double_the_value;}if(sum%10!=0){SWI_disallow=1;}}</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='#MEID_hex'/><tag>SWI_meaning=MEID_hex.V;if(SWI_meaning.length == 15){var mask=[0,2,4,6,8,1,3,5,7,9,5,7,9,'b','d','f'];var sum=0;var double_the_value=0;var i;var add;var allowed;for(i=SWI_meaning.length-1;i>=0;i--){add=parseInt(SWI_meaning[i],16);sum+=double_the_value?parseInt(mask[add],16):add;double_the_value=!double_the_value;}if(sum%16!=0){SWI_disallow=1;}}</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='MEID_dec'><item repeat='10'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item><item repeat='8'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item><item repeat='0-1'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item></rule><rule id='MEID_hex'><one-of><item>a<tag>V='A'</tag></item><item>b<tag>V='B'</tag></item><item>c<tag>V='C'</tag></item><item>d<tag>V='D'</tag></item><item>e<tag>V='E'</tag></item><item>f<tag>V='F'</tag></item></one-of><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#HEX'/><tag>V=V?V+HEX.V:HEX.V</tag><item repeat='6'><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#HEX'/><tag>V=V?V+HEX.V:HEX.V</tag></item><item repeat='6'><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#HEX'/><tag>V=V?V+HEX.V:HEX.V</tag></item><item repeat='0-1'><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#HEX'/><tag>V=V?V+HEX.V:HEX.V</tag></item></rule><rule id='DIGIT'><one-of><item>cero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>uno<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>dos<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>tres<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>cuatro<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>cinco<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>seis<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>siete<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>ocho<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nueve<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The provided GRXML grammar defines a complex validation logic for a MEID (Mobile Equipment Identifier) number, which can be numeric (decimal) or alphanumeric (hexadecimal). This kind of validation and structure is best represented with a regular expression rather than using a closed list entity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: meid\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: meid\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(?:\\d{18,19}|[A-Fa-f0-9]{14,15})$'\n    description: \"Matches MEID (Mobile Equipment Identifier) containing either 18 or 19 numeric digits, or 14-15 hexadecimal characters (letters A-F or digits 0-9).\""}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file meid_2 to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' xml:lang='en-US' root='_meid'><rule id='_meid' scope='public'><item repeat='0-1'>@hes@</item><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#MEID_dec'/><tag>SWI_meaning=MEID_dec.V;if(SWI_meaning.length==19){var mask=[0,2,4,6,8,1,3,5,7,9];var sum=0;var double_the_value=0;var i;var add;for(i=SWI_meaning.length-1;i>=0;i--){add=parseInt(SWI_meaning[i],10);sum+=double_the_value?parseInt(mask[add],10):add;double_the_value=!double_the_value;}if(sum%10!=0){SWI_disallow=1;}}</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='#MEID_hex'/><tag>SWI_meaning=MEID_hex.V;if(SWI_meaning.length==15){var mask=[0,2,4,6,8,1,3,5,7,9,5,7,9,'b','d','f'];var sum=0;var double_the_value=0;var i;var add;for(i=SWI_meaning.length-1;i>=0;i--){add=parseInt(SWI_meaning[i],16);sum+=double_the_value?parseInt(mask[add],16):add;double_the_value=!double_the_value;}if(sum%16!=0){SWI_disallow=1;}}</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='MEID_dec'><item repeat='10'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item><item repeat='8'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item><item repeat='0-1'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item></rule><rule id='MEID_hex'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#ANa'/><tag>V='A'</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#ANb'/><tag>V='B'</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#ANc'/><tag>V='C'</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#ANd'/><tag>V='D'</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#ANe'/><tag>V='E'</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#ANf'/><tag>V='F'</tag></item></one-of><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#HEX'/><tag>V=V?V+HEX.V:HEX.V</tag><item repeat='6'><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#HEX'/><tag>V=V?V+HEX.V:HEX.V</tag></item><item repeat='6'><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#HEX'/><tag>V=V?V+HEX.V:HEX.V</tag></item><item repeat='0-1'><ruleref uri='hexadecimal.grxml#HEX'/><tag>V=V?V+HEX.V:HEX.V</tag></item></rule><rule id='DIGIT'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#ZERO'/><tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>one<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>two<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>three<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>four<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>five<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>seven<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>eight<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nine<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='ZERO'><one-of><item>zero</item><item>oh</item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The GRXML grammar provided represents a mobile equipment identifier (MEID), which can be expressed either in a decimal numeric format (18 or 19 digits) or in a hexadecimal format (14 or 15 characters). The grammar validates specific formatting and check digit rules. Due to its complexity, including variable-length patterns that cannot be captured by a simple prebuilt entity or closed list, the best choice is to define a CustomRegexEntity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: meid_2\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: meid_2\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(?:\\d{18,19}|[A-Fa-f0-9]{14,15})$'\n      isCaseSensitive: false"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file mobile_id_sample_wrapper to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><item><ruleref uri='#vocab'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (vocab.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } SWI_meaning=vocab.SWI_meaning; if(vocab.id_type) {id_type=vocab.id_type}; if(vocab.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=vocab.dm_confirm_string}; if(vocab.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=vocab.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(vocab.dm_command) { dm_command=vocab.dm_command; } else if(vocab.dm_root) { dm_root=vocab.dm_root; } else { dm_root=SWI_meaning; } MEANING=SWI_meaning;</tag></item></rule><rule id='vocab'><one-of><item><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.01'>@hes@</item><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.01'><ruleref uri='#prefixes'/></item><one-of><item weight='1.0'><ruleref uri='imei.grxml#_imei'/><tag>SWI_meaning=_imei.SWI_meaning; if(_imei.id_type) { id_type=_imei.id_type; }</tag></item><item weight='1.0'><ruleref uri='meid.grxml#_meid'/><tag>SWI_meaning=_meid.SWI_meaning; if(_meid.id_type) { id_type=_meid.id_type; }</tag></item><item weight='0.01'><ruleref uri='esn.grxml#_esn'/><tag>SWI_meaning=_esn.SWI_meaning; if(_esn.id_type) { id_type=_esn.id_type; }</tag></item></one-of><tag>dm_confirm_string=SWI_meaning; dm_confirmation_mode='IF_NECESSARY';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='prefixes' scope='private'><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.01'>sí</item><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.1'>okay</item><one-of><item>okay</item><item><item repeat='0-1'><one-of><item>mi</item><item>el</item></one-of></item><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#imei_meid_esn_vocab'/></item><item>número</item></one-of><item repeat='0-1'>es<item repeat='0-1'>el</item></item></item><item>es<item repeat='0-1'>el</item></item><item>sí</item></one-of></rule><rule id='imei_meid_esn_vocab'><item repeat='0-1'>número</item><one-of><item>i_m_e_i</item><item>imei</item><item>m_e_i_d</item><item>e_s_n</item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: |\n  The provided GRXML defines rules for matching device identifiers (IMEI, MEID, ESN). \n  These identifiers follow specific numeric and alphanumeric patterns which are best captured by a regex.\n  The provided grammar references other grammars (imei.grxml, meid.grxml, esn.grxml), indicating that these are structured numeric/alphanumeric identifiers, which typically should be represented as RegexEntity in Copilot Studio.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: mobile_id_sample_wrapper\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: mobile_id_sample_wrapper\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(?:\\d{14,16}|[A-Fa-f0-9]{8,15})$'\n      description: Matches IMEI (numeric 14-16 digits), MEID (hexadecimal 14-15 chars) or ESN (hexadecimal numeric identifiers)."}]}
