></item><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#imei_meid_esn_vocab'/></item><item> number </item></one-of><item repeat='0-1'> is </item></item><item> it's </item><item> yes </item></one-of></rule><rule id='imei_meid_esn_vocab'><one-of><item> i_m_e_i </item><item> imei </item><item> m_e_i_d </item><item> e_s_n </item></one-of><item repeat='0-1'> number </item></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (ClosedListEntity)\nreason: The input grammar defines specific types of identification numbers (IMEI, MEID, ESN) and various synonyms or expressions users might use to refer to these identifiers. It's best mapped as a Custom ClosedListEntity to accurately capture variations and allow synonyms and contextual phrases from the user input.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: mobile_id_sample_wrapper_2\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: mobile_id_sample_wrapper_2\n    entity:\n      kind: ClosedListEntity\n      items:\n        - id: imei\n          displayName: imei\n          synonyms:\n            - i_m_e_i\n        - id: meid\n          displayName: meid\n          synonyms:\n            - m_e_i_d\n        - id: esn\n          displayName: esn\n          synonyms:\n            - e_s_n"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file natnum to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='N'><rule id='N' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#whole_hundreds'/><tag>V = V + whole_hundreds.V;</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='#whole_thousands'/><tag>V = V + whole_thousands.V;</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='whole_hundreds' scope='public'><ruleref uri='#digits_1_9'/><tag>V = digits_1_9.V</tag>hundred<tag>V = V + '00';</tag></rule><rule id='whole_thousands' scope='public'><ruleref uri='#digits_1_9'/><tag>V = digits_1_9.V</tag>thousand<tag>V = V + '000';</tag></rule><rule id='digits_1_9'><one-of><item>one<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>two<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>three<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>four<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>five<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>seven<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>eight<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nine<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Prebuilt entity\nreason: The grammar defines number phrases like \"one hundred\", \"two thousand\", etc., which represent numeric values. Thus, it maps directly to the prebuilt \"Number\" entity provided by Microsoft Copilot Studio.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: PrebuiltEntityComponent\n    displayName: Number\n    prebuiltEntityType: Number\n    state: Active\n    status: Active"}]}
