{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file renumbering_SWI_vars_allow_dtmf to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' mode='dtmf' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='ROOT'><rule id='ROOT' scope='public'><ruleref uri='#DTMFDIGITS'/><tag>var all_commands=['vanilla','chocolate','strawberry','butter_pecan','coffee'];var computed_command_list=[];if(SWI_vars.allow){var inclusion_list=SWI_vars.allow.split('^');computed_command_list=['PLACEHOLDER'];for(var i=0;i&lt;all_commands.length;i++){var include_it=0;for(var j=0;j&lt;inclusion_list.length;j++){if(all_commands[i]==inclusion_list[j]){include_it=1;}}if(include_it==1){computed_command_list.push(all_commands[i]);}}}else{computed_command_list=all_commands;computed_command_list.unshift('PLACEHOLDER');}SWI_meaning=computed_command_list[DTMFDIGITS.SWI_meaning];if(DTMFDIGITS.SWI_meaning&gt;(computed_command_list.length-1)){SWI_disallow=1;}dm_root=SWI_meaning;MEANING=SWI_meaning;</tag></rule><rule id='DTMFDIGITS' scope='public'><one-of><item>1<tag>SWI_meaning=1</tag></item><item>2<tag>SWI_meaning=2</tag></item><item>3<tag>SWI_meaning=3</tag></item><item>4<tag>SWI_meaning=4</tag></item><item>5<tag>SWI_meaning=5</tag></item><item>6<tag>SWI_meaning=6</tag></item><item>7<tag>SWI_meaning=7</tag></item><item>8<tag>SWI_meaning=8</tag></item><item>9<tag>SWI_meaning=9</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomListEntity\nreason: The GRXML grammar is using DTMF input to select between numeric options mapped to ice cream flavor commands. A prebuilt entity doesn't exist for this use case. Hence, you'll need a Closed List Custom Entity mapping numbers to ice cream flavors for user selection.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: renumbering_SWI_vars_allow_dtmf\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: renumbering_SWI_vars_allow_dtmf\n    entity:\n      kind: ClosedListEntity\n      items:\n        - id: '1'\n          displayName: vanilla\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '2'\n          displayName: chocolate\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '3'\n          displayName: strawberry\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '4'\n          displayName: butter pecan\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '5'\n          displayName: coffee\n          synonyms: []"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file renumbering_SWI_vars_disallow_dtmf to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' mode='dtmf' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='ROOT'><rule id='ROOT' scope='public'><ruleref uri='#DTMFDIGITS'/><tag>var all_commands=['vanilla','chocolate','strawberry','butter_pecan','coffee'];var computed_command_list=[];if(SWI_vars.disallow){var exclusion_list=SWI_vars.disallow.split('^');computed_command_list=['PLACEHOLDER'];for(var i=0;i&lt;all_commands.length;i++){var include_it=1;for(var j=0;j&lt;exclusion_list.length;j++){if(all_commands[i]==exclusion_list[j]){include_it=0;}}if(include_it==1){computed_command_list.push(all_commands[i]);}}}else{computed_command_list=all_commands;computed_command_list.unshift('PLACEHOLDER');}SWI_meaning=computed_command_list[DTMFDIGITS.SWI_meaning];if(DTMFDIGITS.SWI_meaning&gt;(computed_command_list.length-1)){SWI_disallow=1;}dm_root=SWI_meaning;MEANING=SWI_meaning;</tag></rule><rule id='DTMFDIGITS' scope='public'><one-of><item>1<tag>SWI_meaning=1</tag></item><item>2<tag>SWI_meaning=2</tag></item><item>3<tag>SWI_meaning=3</tag></item><item>4<tag>SWI_meaning=4</tag></item><item>5<tag>SWI_meaning=5</tag></item><item>6<tag>SWI_meaning=6</tag></item><item>7<tag>SWI_meaning=7</tag></item><item>8<tag>SWI_meaning=8</tag></item><item>9<tag>SWI_meaning=9</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomListEntity\\nreason: The provided GRXML grammar represents a selection using DTMF numerical entry, mapping digits to ice cream flavor choices with logic for exclusions. Because Copilot Studio does not directly support scripting or dynamic exclusions in entities, implement this as a CustomListEntity to handle digit-to-flavor mapping explicitly without scripting logic. Dynamic exclusion logic can be handled instead using dialog or conditional logic within Copilot Studio's canvas or flow designer.\\ncopilot_studio_code: |\\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\\n    displayName: renumbering_SWI_vars_disallow_dtmf\\n    state: Active\\n    status: Active\\n    schemaName: renumbering_SWI_vars_disallow_dtmf\\n    entity:\\n      kind: ClosedListEntity\\n      items:\\n        - id: \\\"1\\\"\\n          displayName: vanilla\\n          synonyms:\\n            - 1\\n        - id: \\\"2\\\"\\n          displayName: chocolate\\n          synonyms:\\n            - 2\\n        - id: \\\"3\\\"\\n          displayName: strawberry\\n          synonyms:\\n            - 3\\n        - id: \\\"4\\\"\\n          displayName: butter_pecan\\n          synonyms:\\n            - 4\\n        - id: \\\"5\\\"\\n          displayName: coffee\\n          synonyms:\\n            - 5"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file socialsecurity to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' xml:lang='es-US' root='_socialsecurity'><rule id='_socialsecurity' scope='public'><item repeat='0-1'>@hes@</item><ruleref uri='#NineDigits_3_2_4'/><tag>SWI_meaning = NineDigits_3_2_4.VALUE; if(typeof(NineDigits_3_2_4.is_natnum) != 'undefined'){is_natnum=NineDigits_3_2_4.is_natnum;} var area=parseInt(SWI_meaning.substr(0,3),10); var group=SWI_meaning.substr(3,2); var serial=SWI_meaning.substr(5,4); if(group=='00'){SWI_disallow=1;} if(serial=='0000'){SWI_disallow=1;} if(area==0||area==666||area>=900){SWI_disallow=1;} MEANING=SWI_meaning;</tag></rule><rule id='NineDigits_3_2_4'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#D_1_1'/><ruleref uri='#DD_1_2'/></item><item><ruleref uri='#DDD_3_3'/></item></one-of><ruleref uri='#DD_1_2'/><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#DD_1_2'/><ruleref uri='#DD_1_2'/></item><item><ruleref uri='#N1000_9999'/></item></one-of></rule><rule id='DD_1_2'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#N0_9'/><ruleref uri='#N0_9'/></item><item><ruleref uri='#N10_99'/></item></one-of></rule><rule id='D_1_1'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#N0_9'/></item></one-of></rule><rule id='DDD_3_3'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#N100_999'/></item></one-of></rule><rule id='N1000_9999'><one-of><item>mil</item><item><ruleref uri='#N2_9_mil'/>mil</item><item><one-of><item><tag>VALUE=1</tag>mil</item><item><ruleref uri='#N2_9_mil'/>mil</item></one-of><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#N100_999'/></item><item><ruleref uri='#N10_99'/></item><item><ruleref uri='#N0_9'/></item></one-of></item></one-of></rule><rule id='N100_999'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#hundreds'/></item><item><ruleref uri='#hundreds2'/><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#N10_99'/></item><item><ruleref uri='#N0_9'/></item></one-of></item></one-of></rule><rule id='N0_9'><one-of><item><tag>VALUE=0</tag>cero</item><item><tag>VALUE=1</tag>uno</item><item><tag>VALUE=2</tag>dos</item><item><tag>VALUE=3</tag>tres</item><item><tag>VALUE=4</tag>cuatro</item><item><tag>VALUE=5</tag>cinco</item><item><tag>VALUE=6</tag>seis</item><item><tag>VALUE=7</tag>siete</item><item><tag>VALUE=8</tag>ocho</item><item><tag>VALUE=9</tag>nueve</item></one-of></rule><rule id='N10_99'><one-of><item><tag>VALUE=10</tag>diez</item><item><tag>VALUE=11</tag>once</item><item><tag>VALUE=12</tag>doce</item><item><tag>VALUE=13</tag>trece</item><item><tag>VALUE=14</tag>catorce</item><item><tag>VALUE=15</tag>quince</item><item><tag>VALUE=16</tag>dieciséis</item><item><tag>VALUE=17</tag>diecisiete</item><item><tag>VALUE=18</tag>dieciocho</item><item><tag>VALUE=19</tag>diecinueve</item><item><tag>VALUE=20</tag>veinte</item><item><tag>VALUE=21</tag>veintiuno</item><item><tag>VALUE=22</tag>veintidós</item><item><tag>VALUE=23</tag>veintitrés</item><item><tag>VALUE=24</tag>veinticuatro</item><item><tag>VALUE=25</tag>veinticinco</item><item><tag>VALUE=26</tag>veintiséis</item><item><tag>VALUE=27</tag>veintisiete</item><item><tag>VALUE=28</tag>veintiocho</item><item><tag>VALUE=29</tag>veintinueve</item><item><tag>VALUE=30</tag>treinta</item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: RegexEntity\nreason: The provided GRXML grammar contains rules to recognize and validate a specific numeric format, specifically a Social Security number (SSN). Due to detailed numeric validation logic (such as disallowing invalid area numbers, group and serial formats), this is best handled as a Regular Expression (Regex) entity within Copilot Studio, rather than a ClosedListEntity or Prebuilt entity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: socialsecurity\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: socialsecurity\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(?!000|666|9\\d{2})(\\d{3})(?!00)(\\d{2})(?!0000)(\\d{4})$'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file socialsecurity_1 to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' xml:lang='en-US' root='socialsecurity'><rule id='socialsecurity' scope='public'><item><ruleref uri='#SSN'/><tag>var ssn=SSN.V; var invalid_treatment = 'disallow'; var area = parseInt (ssn.substr(0,3), 10); var group = ssn.substr (3,2); var serial = ssn.substr (5,4); if (group == '00' || serial == '0000' || area == 0 || area == 666 || area >= 900) { if (invalid_treatment == 'disallow') { SWI_disallow=1; } else { ssn = invalid_treatment; } } socialsecurity=ssn;</tag></item></rule><rule id='SSN'><ruleref uri='#AREA'/><tag>V=V?V+AREA.V:AREA.V</tag><ruleref uri='#GROUP'/><tag>V=V?V+GROUP.V:GROUP.V</tag><ruleref uri='#SERIAL'/><tag>V=V?V+SERIAL.V:SERIAL.V</tag></rule><rule id='AREA'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag><one-of><item><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item></item><item><ruleref uri='#twodigits'/><tag>V+=''+twodigits.digits</tag></item><item><tag>V+='00'</tag>hundred</item></one-of></rule><rule id='GROUP'><one-of><item><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item></item><item><ruleref uri='#twodigits'/><tag>V=''+twodigits.digits</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='SERIAL'><one-of><item><item repeat='4'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item></item><item><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='#twodigits'/><tag>V=V?V+twodigits.digits:''+twodigits.digits</tag></item></item><item><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item><ruleref uri='#twodigits'/><tag>V=V?V+twodigits.digits:''+twodigits.digits</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='#twodigits'/><tag>V=V?V+twodigits.digits:''+twodigits.digits</tag><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item></item><item><one-of><item><tag>V='1100'</tag>eleven</item><item><tag>V='1200'</tag>twelve</item><item><tag>V='1300'</tag>thirteen</item><item><tag>V='1400'</tag>fourteen</item><item><tag>V='1500'</tag>fifteen</item><item><tag>V='1600'</tag>sixteen</item><item><tag>V='1700'</tag>seventeen</item><item><tag>V='1800'</tag>eighteen</item><item><tag>V='1900'</tag>nineteen</item><item><ruleref uri='#tens'/><tag>V=tens.digit</tag><ruleref uri='#digit19'/><tag>V+=''+digit19.digit+'00'</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='#TensWithDash'/><tag>V=TensWithDash.VALUE+'00';</tag></item></one-of></item><item><ruleref uri='#digit19'/><tag>V=digit19.digit+'000'</tag>thousand</item></one-of></rule><rule id='DIGIT'><one-of><item><tag>V='0'</tag>oh</item><item><tag>V='0'</tag>zero</item><item><tag>V='1'</tag>one</item><item><tag>V='2'</tag>two</item><item><tag>V='3'</tag>three</item><item><tag>V='4'</tag>four</item><item><tag>V='5'</tag>five</item><item><tag>V='6'</tag>six</item><item><tag>V='7'</tag>seven</item><item><tag>V='8'</tag>eight</item><item><tag>V='9'</tag>nine</item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Prebuilt entity\nreason: \"The provided GRXML grammar explicitly represents and validates social security numbers, which aligns with the prebuilt entity 'Number' or numeric combinations provided by Microsoft Copilot Studio. However, because of the specific structure validation and formatting of a US Social Security Number (SSN), you should represent this entity as a 'RegexEntity' to ensure precise pattern matching and validation.\"\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: SocialSecurityNumber\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: SocialSecurityNumber\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(?!000|666|9\\d{2})\\d{3}(?!00)\\d{2}(?!0000)\\d{4}$'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file socialsecurity_2 to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' xml:lang='en-US' root='_socialsecurity'><rule id='_socialsecurity' scope='public'><item repeat='0-1'>@hes@</item><item><ruleref uri='#SSN'/><tag>SWI_meaning=SSN.V; var area=parseInt(SWI_meaning.substr(0,3),10); var group=SWI_meaning.substr(3,2); var serial=SWI_meaning.substr(5,4); if(group=='00'){SWI_disallow=1;} if(serial=='0000'){SWI_disallow=1;} if(area==0||area==666||area>=900){SWI_disallow=1;} MEANING=SWI_meaning;</tag></item></rule><rule id='SSN'><item repeat='9'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V=V?V+DIGIT.V:DIGIT.V</tag></item></rule><rule id='DIGIT'><one-of><item>zero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>oh<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>one<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>two<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>three<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>four<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>five<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>seven<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>eight<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nine<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Prebuilt entity\nreason: The provided grammar extracts a social security number (SSN). Microsoft Copilot Studio has a prebuilt entity \\\"Number\\\" suitable for digit-based sequences. However, due to specific formatting and validation rules (checking valid SSN ranges and excluding invalid digit groups), it's advisable to use a RegexEntity to enforce accuracy. The existing grammar validates SSNs, which is more precise than generic number extraction.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: socialsecurity\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: socialsecurity\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '(?!000|666|9\\d\\d)(\\d{3})(?!00)(\\d{2})(?!0000)(\\d{4})'\n      description: Matches valid US Social Security Numbers while excluding invalid numbers according to SSA guidelines."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file soundexDOB to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='S'><rule id='S' scope='public'><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><tag>if (parseInt(V,10) &gt; 984){SWI_disallow=1;}</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The GRXML grammar specifies exactly three digits (with numeric validation <=984); this numeric and range validation can be translated into a regular expression entity for validation more effectively.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: soundexDOB\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: soundexDOB\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(?:[0-8]\\d{2}|9[0-7]\\d|98[0-4])$'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file soundexDOB_2 to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='S'><rule id='S' scope='public'><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><tag>if (parseInt(V,10) &gt; 984){ SWI_disallow=1; }</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The grammar specifies exactly 3 digits, along with logic to restrict the range (001 to 984). This type of numeric pattern with constraint validation cannot be handled by prebuilt entities directly and should be handled using a regex entity to represent a three-digit numeric pattern (000-999). The additional range logic (V>984) must subsequently be validated through custom code after the regex match.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: soundexDOB_2\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: soundexDOB_2\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^\\d{3}$'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file soundexLastName to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='S'><rule id='S' scope='public'><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><item repeat='0-1'><ruleref uri='special_chars.grxml#dash'/></item><one-of><item><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='#D6'/><tag>V = V ? V + D6.V : D6.V;</tag></item></item><item><ruleref uri='#D6'/><tag>V = V ? V + D6.V : D6.V;</tag><ruleref uri='#N10_66'/><tag>V = V + N10_66.V ;</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='#N100_600'/><tag>V = V + N100_600.V ;</tag></item></one-of><tag>if( ( (V.substring(1,2) == '0') &amp;&amp; (V.substring(2,4) != '00') ) || ( (V.substring(2,3) == '0') &amp;&amp; (V.substring(3,4) != '0') ) ) { SWI_disallow = 1; }</tag></rule><rule id='D6'><one-of><item>cero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>uno<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>dos<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>tres<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>cuatro<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>cinco<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>seis<tag>V='6'</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='N10_66' scope='public'><one-of><item>diez<tag>V='10';</tag></item><item>once<tag>V='11';</tag></item><item>doce<tag>V='12';</tag></item><item>trece<tag>V='13';</tag></item><item>catorce<tag>V='14';</tag></item><item>quince<tag>V='15';</tag></item><item>dieciséis<tag>V='16';</tag></item><item>veinte<tag>V='20';</tag></item><item>veintiuno<tag>V='21';</tag></item><item>veintidós<tag>V='22';</tag></item><item>veintitrés<tag>V='23';</tag></item><item>veinticuatro<tag>V='24';</tag></item><item>veinticinco<tag>V='25';</tag></item><item>veintiséis<tag>V='26';</tag></item><item>treinta<tag>V='30';</tag></item><item>treinta_y_uno<tag>V='31';</tag></item><item>treinta_y_dos<tag>V='32';</tag></item><item>treinta_y_tres<tag>V='33';</tag></item><item>treinta_y_cuatro<tag>V='34';</tag></item><item>treinta_y_cinco<tag>V='35';</tag></item><item>treinta_y_seis<tag>V='36';</tag></item><item>cuarent