{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file checking_account_number_wrapper to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><ruleref uri='#vocab'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (vocab.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } SWI_meaning=vocab.SWI_meaning; if(vocab.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=vocab.dm_confirm_string}; if(vocab.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=vocab.dm_confirmation_mode}; dm_root=vocab.SWI_meaning; MEANING=SWI_meaning;</tag></rule><rule id='vocab'><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.01'>@hes@</item><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.01'><ruleref uri='#prefixes'/></item><ruleref uri='checking_account_number.grxml#checking_account_number'/><tag>SWI_meaning = checking_account_number.SWI_meaning; dm_confirm_string = SWI_meaning; dm_confirmation_mode='IF_NECESSARY';</tag></rule><rule id='prefixes' scope='private'><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.01'>yes</item><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.1'>okay</item><item repeat='0-1' repeat-prob='0.01'><one-of><item>let me see</item><item>let's see</item></one-of></item><one-of><item>okay</item><item><item repeat='0-1'><one-of><item>my</item><item>the</item></one-of></item><one-of><item><item repeat='0-1'><ruleref uri='#account_type'/></item><item repeat='0-1'>account</item>number</item><item><ruleref uri='#account_type'/><item repeat='0-1'>account</item></item><item>account</item></one-of><item repeat='0-1'>is</item></item><item>it's</item><item>yes</item></one-of></rule><rule id='account_type' scope='private'><one-of><item>checking</item><item>savings</item><item>bank</item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom entity (RegexEntity)\\nreason: The grammar intended for \\\"checking account number\\\" input references directly an external GRXML file (\\\"checking_account_number.grxml\\\") that likely represents a numerical format (numbers for an account). Such numerical data is best handled through regular expressions in Copilot Studio instead of a closed synonym list.\\ncopilot_studio_code: |\\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\\n    displayName: checking_account_number\\n    state: Active\\n    status: Active\\n    schemaName: checking_account_number\\n    entity:\\n      kind: RegexEntity\\n      regexPattern: '^[0-9]{4,17}$'\\n      validationMessage: 'Please provide a valid checking account number consisting of 4 to 17 digits.'\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The provided grammar references a \\\"checking_account_number\\\" in an external grammar file, apparently designed for numeric input such as account numbers. Typically, account numbers are numeric with varying digit-lengths. Therefore, implementing it as a Regular Expression entity in Copilot Studio is the most practical solution, allowing flexible numeric input validation.\\n- Prefixes or introductory phrases such as \\\"my account number is,\\\" \\\"it is,\\\" \\\"checking account,\\\" etc. are not part of the numeric validation variable itself. Instead, these are usually captured through conversational logic rather than entity definitions. Thus, the main entity extracted here remains numeric, matching a regex suitable for account numbers."}]}
