{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file digit(1) to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='D'><rule id='D' scope='public'><one-of><item>oh<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>zero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>one<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>two<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>three<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>four<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>five<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>seven<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>eight<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nine<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomListEntity\nreason: The entity represents digits with interchangeable synonyms (e.g., \\\"oh\\\" and \\\"zero\\\" both map to digit \\\"0\\\"), so it is best represented as a ClosedListEntity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: digit\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: digit\n    entity:\n      kind: ClosedListEntity\n      items:\n        - id: '0'\n          displayName: '0'\n          synonyms:\n            - oh\n            - zero\n        - id: '1'\n          displayName: '1'\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '2'\n          displayName: '2'\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '3'\n          displayName: '3'\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '4'\n          displayName: '4'\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '5'\n          displayName: '5'\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '6'\n          displayName: '6'\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '7'\n          displayName: '7'\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '8'\n          displayName: '8'\n          synonyms: []\n        - id: '9'\n          displayName: '9'\n          synonyms: []"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file digit to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='D'><rule id='D' scope='public'><one-of><item>cero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>uno<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>dos<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>tres<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>cuatro<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>cinco<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>seis<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>siete<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>ocho<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nueve<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomListEntity\\nreason: The grammar defines a precise set of Spanish spoken digits (\\\"cero\\\" to \\\"nueve\\\"), which fits best as a ClosedListEntity, specifying exact mapping between spoken digit and numeric value.\\ncopilot_studio_code: |\\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\\n    displayName: digit\\n    state: Active\\n    status: Active\\n    schemaName: digit\\n    entity:\\n      kind: ClosedListEntity\\n      items:\\n        - id: '0'\\n          displayName: cero\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '1'\\n          displayName: uno\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '2'\\n          displayName: dos\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '3'\\n          displayName: tres\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '4'\\n          displayName: cuatro\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '5'\\n          displayName: cinco\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '6'\\n          displayName: seis\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '7'\\n          displayName: siete\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '8'\\n          displayName: ocho\\n          synonyms: []\\n        - id: '9'\\n          displayName: nueve\\n          synonyms: []"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file digits_1 to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-gb' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='digits'><rule id='digits' scope='public'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT_SEQUENCE'/></rule><rule id='DIGIT_SEQUENCE'><item repeat='4'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V = V ? V + DIGIT.V : DIGIT.V</tag></item></rule><rule id='DIGIT'><one-of><item>oh<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>zero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>null<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>nil<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>nought<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>one<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>two<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>three<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>four<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>five<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>seven<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>eight<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nine<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: RegexEntity\nreason: The grammar specifies a fixed-length numeric sequence (exactly 4 digits) where digits can have multiple spoken synonyms. Copilot Studio does not directly support spoken synonyms for numeric digits within a single prebuilt entity. Therefore, the best choice is creating a RegexEntity, as this accurately defines the numeric format expected.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: digits_1\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: digits_1\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file digits_2 to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='digits'><rule id='digits' scope='public'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT_SEQUENCE'/><tag> digits = DIGIT_SEQUENCE.V; </tag></rule><rule id='DIGIT_SEQUENCE'><item repeat='4'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V = V ? V + DIGIT.V : DIGIT.V</tag></item></rule><rule id='DIGIT'><one-of><item>oh<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>zero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>one<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>two<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>three<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>four<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>five<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>seven<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>eight<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nine<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom RegexEntity\nreason: The GRXML represents a sequence of digits, each digit mapped from spoken words to numeric characters specifically (e.g., 'oh'/'zero' mapped to '0'). Since Microsoft Copilot Studio doesn't have a built-in entity enforcing exactly four digit inputs via spoken words, this grammar is best represented as a custom regex entity enforcing a four-digit numeric input.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: digits_2\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: digits_2\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^\\d{4}$'"}]}
