{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file digits_4_1 to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='fr-fr' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='digits'><rule id='digits' scope='public'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT_SEQUENCE'/><tag>digits = DIGIT_SEQUENCE.V;</tag></rule><rule id='DIGIT_SEQUENCE'><item repeat='4'><ruleref uri='#DIGIT'/><tag>V = V ? V + DIGIT.V : DIGIT.V</tag></item></rule><rule id='DIGIT'><one-of><item>zero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>zéro<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>un<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>deux<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>trois<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>quatre<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>cinq<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>sept<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>huit<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>neuf<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom Regex Entity\nreason: The provided GRXML represents a digit sequence of exactly 4 digits spoken in French. This structure is best represented by a regex to enforce exactly four numeric digits. A ClosedListEntity wouldn't effectively capture sequences and constraints on length and digit values.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: digits_4_1\n    state: Active\n    schemaName: digits_4_1\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'"}]}
