{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_AB(1) to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; if (SWI_meaning.substring(0,1) == 'O' || SWI_meaning.substring(0,1) == 'I'){SWI_disallow=1;} ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_enus_drivers_license_AB';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><one-of><item repeat='5-9'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + A.V : A.V;</tag><item repeat='5'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><item>a<tag>V='A'</tag></item><ruleref uri='#Aset'/><tag>V = V ? V + Aset.V : Aset.V;</tag><item repeat='4'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule><rule id='Aset'><one-of><item>a<tag>V='A'</tag></item><item>b<tag>V='B'</tag></item><item>c<tag>V='C'</tag></item><item>d<tag>V='D'</tag></item><item>e<tag>V='E'</tag></item><item>f<tag>V='F'</tag></item><item>g<tag>V='G'</tag></item><item>h<tag>V='H'</tag></item><item>j<tag>V='J'</tag></item><item>k<tag>V='K'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The provided GRXML content describes an alphanumeric license number format that includes repeating patterns of digits and letters. Therefore, it should be implemented as a Custom Regex Entity, as this allows the flexibility needed to capture the patterns precisely.  \ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_AB\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_AB\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '(([0-9]{5,9})|([A-Za-z][0-9]{5})|(A[A-HJ-K][0-9]{4}))'\n      validationErrorMessage: 'Please enter a valid license number.'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_AB to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) {               var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^');               disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow;               for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) {                 if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) {                   SWI_disallow=1;                   break;                 }               }              }            if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;};            if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command};            if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode};            if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string};            grammar_version='20180502';            MEANING=SWI_meaning;            if (SWI_meaning.substring(0,1) == 'O' || SWI_meaning.substring(0,1) == 'I'){SWI_disallow=1;}          ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_esus_drivers_license_AB';        </tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><one-of><item repeat='5-9'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + A.V : A.V;</tag><item repeat='5'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><item>a<tag>V='A'</tag></item><ruleref uri='#Aset'/><tag>V = V ? V + Aset.V : Aset.V;</tag><item repeat='4'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule><rule id='Aset'><one-of><item>a<tag>V='A'</tag></item><item>b<tag>V='B'</tag></item><item>c<tag>V='C'</tag></item><item>d<tag>V='D'</tag></item><item>e<tag>V='E'</tag></item><item>f<tag>V='F'</tag></item><item>g<tag>V='G'</tag></item><item>h<tag>V='H'</tag></item><item>j<tag>V='J'</tag></item><item>k<tag>V='K'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom RegexEntity\nreason: The GRXML defines a driver's license pattern involving alphabets and digits with specific repetition patterns, matching a well-defined alphanumeric structure. It is suitable for converting to regular expressions to accurately validate the specific driver's license formats.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_AB\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_AB\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '(^[0-9]{5,9}$)|(^[A-Za-z]{1}[0-9]{5}$)|(^A[A-HJ-K]{1}[0-9]{4}$)'\n      isCaseSensitive: false\n      isAccentSensitive: false"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_AK(1) to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_enus_drivers_license_AK';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license'><item><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#D7'/><tag>V = V ? V + D7.V : D7.V;</tag><item repeat='6'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><one-of><item>eight<tag>V = 8;</tag></item><item>nine<tag>V = 8;</tag></item></one-of><item repeat='6'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><item repeat='1-6'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule><rule id='D7'><one-of><item>oh<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>zero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>one<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>two<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>three<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>four<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>five<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>seven<tag>V='7'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom RegexEntity\nreason: The GRXML grammar describes patterns of spoken Alaska driver's license numbers, consisting primarily of numeric digits and interpretations (e.g., 'oh' as 0). This lends itself naturally to a Regex entity, as the numeric sequences follow fixed-length digit formats (1 to 7 numeric digits).\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: AlaskaDriversLicenseNumber\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: AlaskaDriversLicenseNumber\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^\\d{1,7}$'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_AK to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_esus_drivers_license_AK';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license'><item><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#D7'/><tag>V = V ? V + D7.V : D7.V;</tag><item repeat='6'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><one-of><item>ocho<tag>V = 8;</tag></item><item>nueve<tag>V = 8;</tag></item></one-of><item repeat='6'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><item repeat='1-6' repeat-prob='0.99'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule><rule id='D7'><one-of><item>cero<tag>V='0'</tag></item><item>uno<tag>V='1'</tag></item><item>dos<tag>V='2'</tag></item><item>tres<tag>V='3'</tag></item><item>cuatro<tag>V='4'</tag></item><item>cinco<tag>V='5'</tag></item><item>seis<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>siete<tag>V='7'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (RegexEntity)\nreason: |\n  The provided GRXML defines a driver's license number pattern using explicit digit rules and repeating digits. This pattern cannot be directly mapped as a prebuilt entity or a closed list entity. Instead, it should be represented via a Custom Regex Entity in Copilot Studio to accurately capture the numeric sequences, including specific patterns involving digits and repetitions.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_AK\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_AK\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^[0-9]{1,7}$'\n      description: \"Driver's license number matching 1 to 7 digit numeric sequence for AK license in es-US locale.\""}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_AL(1) to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_enus_drivers_license_AL';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><one-of><item><item repeat='7'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><item repeat='8'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><item><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml#ANi'/><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml#ANd'/><tag>V = 'ID'</tag></item><item repeat='5'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml#ANi'/><tag>V = 'I'</tag><item repeat='6-7'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom entity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The provided GRXML grammar describes specific patterns for Alabama driver license formats using a mix of alphabetical characters and digits with fixed or variable lengths. Since these patterns would not map directly to a prebuilt entity and involve specific numeric and alphabetic format constraints, it is optimal to represent them as Regular Expression (Regex) entities in Copilot Studio.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_AL\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_AL\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '(^(\u005Cd{7}|\u005Cd{8}|[A-Za-z]{2}\u005Cd{5}|[A-Za-z]\u005Cd{6,7})$)'\n    comments: >\n      Regex Explanation:\n        - \\d{7}: Exactly seven digits\n        - \\d{8}: Exactly eight digits\n        - [A-Za-z]{2}\\d{5}: Exactly two letters followed by five digits\n        - [A-Za-z]\\d{6,7}: Exactly one letter followed by six or seven digits\n      This pattern ensures that the entity matches all variants defined in the original GRXML grammar rules for Alabama driver license formats."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_AL to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_esus_drivers_license_AL';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><one-of><item><item repeat='7'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><item repeat='8'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item><item>i d<tag>V = 'ID'</tag></item><item repeat='5'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><item>i<tag>V = 'I'</tag><item repeat='6-7'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The grammar describes license number patterns combining letters ('I', 'ID') followed by digits, as well as purely numeric sequences of fixed length. Since the pattern contains combinations of alphabetic prefixes followed by numeric digits, it is best represented as a Regex custom entity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_AL\n    state: Ac