tem><item>four<tag>V = V ? V + '4' : '4';</tag></item></one-of></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The provided grammar represents specific driver's license numbers formed by numeric patterns including certain prefixes ('98' and '99') or numeric patterns corresponding to months ('01' to '12') and special month+12 codes ('13' to '24'), followed by exactly 7 additional digits. It can best be modeled as a RegexEntity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_CT\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_CT\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(0[1-9]|1[0-9]|2[0-4]|98|99)\\d{7}$'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_CT to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_esus_drivers_license_CT';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><item><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#MonthAndPlusTwelve'/><tag>V = MonthAndPlusTwelve.V;</tag></item><item>nueve ocho<tag>V = '98';</tag></item><item>nueve nueve<tag>V = '99';</tag></item></one-of><item repeat='7'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule><rule id='MonthAndPlusTwelve'><one-of><item>cero<tag>V = V ? V + '0' : '0';</tag><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DnoZero'/><tag>V = V ? V + DnoZero.V : DnoZero.V;</tag></item><item>uno<tag>V = V ? V + '1' : '1';</tag><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><item>dos<tag>V = V ? V + '2' : '2';</tag><one-of><item>cero<tag>V = V ? V + '0' : '0';</tag></item><item>uno<tag>V = V ? V + '1' : '1';</tag></item><item>dos<tag>V = V ? V + '2' : '2';</tag></item><item>tres<tag>V = V ? V + '3' : '3';</tag></item><item>cuatro<tag>V = V ? V + '4' : '4';</tag></item></one-of></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\\nreason: The provided GRXML grammar represents a driver's license number following a fixed pattern combining specific numeric prefixes and a defined length of digits. Given this complexity, the most suitable mapping in Copilot Studio is a Custom Regex-based entity to handle numeric patterns precisely, rather than a closed list of alternatives.\\ncopilot_studio_code: |\\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\\n    displayName: DL_CT\\n    state: Active\\n    status: Active\\n    schemaName: DL_CT\\n    entity:\\n      kind: RegexEntity\\n      regexPattern: '^(0[1-9]|1[0-9]|2[0-4]|98|99)[0-9]{7}$'\\n    description: >\\n      Matches the format for driver's license numbers. The pattern consists of either:\\n      - '0' followed by digits 1-9 (e.g., '01','09'), or\\n      - '1' followed by any digit (e.g., '10','19'), or\\n      - '2' followed by digits 0-4 (e.g., '20','24'), or\\n      - special fixed prefixes '98' or '99',\\n      followed by exactly 7 numeric digits."}]}
