-of><tag>SWI_meaning = V;</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The provided grammar defines specific patterns for Hawaii driver's licenses. It uses combinations of letters and digits following certain defined patterns. Such specific alphanumeric patterns with optional dashes are best represented as a RegexEntity within Microsoft Copilot Studio.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: HawaiiDriversLicense\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: HawaiiDriversLicense\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^(H\\d{8}|\\d{3}-?\\d{2}-?\\d{4}|(AS)?\\d{8}|[A-Za-z]\\d{7})$'"}]}
