mmar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The grammar defines a pattern for recognizing a Manitoba driver's license number, which includes a combination of fixed-length alphabets, digits, and potentially starred (*) characters. Such structures cannot map to standard prebuilt entities or simple lists. For capturing this complex alphanumeric structure, the best choice is a Custom Regex entity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: ManitobaDriversLicense\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: ManitobaDriversLicense\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^([A-Za-z*]{5}[A-Za-z][A-Za-z*]\\d{2}[A-Za-z0-9]{3})$'"}]}
