:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^\\d{7}[a-zA-Z\\*]?$'\n      isCaseSensitive: false"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_MI(1) to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_enus_drivers_license_MI';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><one-of><item><one-of><item><ruleref uri='soundexLastName.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + A.V : A.V;</tag><item>seven two<tag>V = V ? V + '72' : '72';</tag></item><ruleref uri='#D6to9'/><tag>V = V ? V + D6to9.V : D6to9.V;</tag></item></one-of><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><ruleref uri='soundexDOB.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag></item><item weight='0.01'><ruleref uri='soundexLastName.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><ruleref uri='soundexDOB.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></one-of><tag>SWI_meaning = V;</tag></rule><rule id='D6to9'><one-of><item>six<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>seven<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>eight<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nine<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The provided grammar corresponds to a Michigan Driver's License number format, which mixes letters and digits in specific patterns; this is best represented using a regex entity in Copilot Studio. The referenced soundexLastName/DOB and digit sequences indicate a fixed alphanumeric pattern better captured through regular expressions.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_MI\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_MI\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: \"^[A-Z][0-9]{12}$|^[A-Z][A-Z]72[6-9][0-9]{6}[A-Z][0-9]{3}$\"\n    explanation: \"Matches Michigan Driver's License formats; either one letter followed by 12 digits, or two letters followed by '72', a digit from 6-9, followed by 6 digits, one letter, and 3 digits.\""}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_MI to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_esus_drivers_license_MI';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><one-of><item weight='1.0'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='soundexLastName.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + A.V : A.V;</tag><item>siete dos<tag>V = V ? V + '72' : '72';</tag></item><ruleref uri='#D6to9'/><tag>V = V ? V + D6to9.V : D6to9.V;</tag></item></one-of><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><ruleref uri='soundexDOB.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag></item><item weight='0.01'><ruleref uri='soundexLastName.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><ruleref uri='soundexDOB.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></one-of><tag>SWI_meaning = V;</tag></rule><rule id='D6to9'><one-of><item>seis<tag>V='6'</tag></item><item>siete<tag>V='7'</tag></item><item>ocho<tag>V='8'</tag></item><item>nueve<tag>V='9'</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The provided GRXML grammar describes a structured format for recognizing driver's license information, combining alphabetic names, numeric sequences, and date-related soundex formats. Due to the complexity, structure, and combination of individual components (letters, digits, specific digit ranges, and custom references), it is best represented by using regular expressions or custom validation logic as a RegexEntity rather than a simple prebuilt or closed list entity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_MI\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_MI\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '[A-Z]{1,}[0-9]{8,}[A-Z0-9]{1,}' \n      isCaseSensitive: false\n      isMultiline: false\n\nExplanation of regexPattern:  \n- [A-Z]{1,}: captures letters or encoded soundex values at the start (like the soundexLastName).\n- [0-9]{8,}: next digits, including specific numeric sequences described in the grammar.\n- [A-Z0-9]{1,}: end portion can include date cues or another alphanumeric combination as represented by the soundexDOB.\n\nNote: Given complexity and external references to soundex and 'alpha' grammars (which cannot be directly represented), this regex offers a simplified initial mapping. You should further adjust and validate the regex accordingly based on the exact expected inputs."}]}
