{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_NJ(1) to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_enus_drivers_license_NJ';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + A.V : A.V;</tag><item repeat='9'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><ruleref uri='#GenderedMOY'/><tag>V = V ? V + GenderedMOY.V : GenderedMOY.V;</tag><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule><rule id='GenderedMOY' scope='public'><one-of><item><one-of><item>five<tag>V = V ? V + '5' : '5';</tag></item><item>oh<tag>V = V ? V + '0' : '0';</tag></item><item>zero<tag>V = V ? V + '0' : '0';</tag></item></one-of><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DnoZero'/><tag>V = V ? V + DnoZero.V : DnoZero.V;</tag></item><item><one-of><item>six<tag>V = V ? V + '6' : '6';</tag></item><item>one<tag>V = V ? V + '1' : '1';</tag></item></one-of><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DltThree'/><tag>V = V ? V + DltThree.V : DltThree.V;</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The GRXML represents a structured alphanumeric pattern, consisting of a letter followed by specific digits and characters in a fixed pattern. This is best modeled as a regular expression (RegexEntity) to precisely match the structured New Jersey driver's license number format.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_NJ\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_NJ\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^[A-Za-z][0-9]{9}[0156][0-9]{3}$' \n    # Explanation of regex:\n    # ^ = Start of input\n    # [A-Za-z] = Single alphabetic character\n    # [0-9]{9} = Exactly nine digits\n    # [0156] = One digit which can only be either 0,1,5 or 6\n    # [0-9]{3} = Exactly three digits after\n    # $ = End of input"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_NJ to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_esus_drivers_license_NJ';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><ruleref uri='alpha.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + A.V : A.V;</tag><item repeat='9'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><ruleref uri='#GenderedMOY'/><tag>V = V ? V + GenderedMOY.V : GenderedMOY.V;</tag><item repeat='3'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule><rule id='GenderedMOY' scope='public'><one-of><item><one-of><item>cinco<tag>V = V ? V + '5' : '5';</tag></item><item>cero<tag>V = V ? V + '0' : '0';</tag></item></one-of><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DnoZero'/><tag>V = V ? V + DnoZero.V : DnoZero.V;</tag></item><item><one-of><item>seis<tag>V = V ? V + '6' : '6';</tag></item><item>uno<tag>V = V ? V + '1' : '1';</tag></item></one-of><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DltThree'/><tag>V = V ? V + DltThree.V : DltThree.V;</tag></item></one-of></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: Custom entity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The grammar describes a structured alphanumeric sequence (driver's license number) with a specific format: one alphabetic character followed by nine digits, then two digits representing month/gender-specific digits, finishing with three digits. This kind of precise formatting and sequencing is best handled as a Regex entity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_NJ\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_NJ\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^[A-Za-z]\\d{9}(0[1-9]|[12][0-3]|5[1-9]|6[0-3])\\d{3}$'"}]}
