{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_QC(1) to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='en-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; if (SWI_meaning.substring(4,5) === '0'){SWI_disallow=1;} ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_enus_drivers_license_QC';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><ruleref uri='soundexLastName.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag><one-of><item>nine nine nine nine nine nine<tag>V = V ? V + '999999' : '999999';</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DayOfMonth'/><tag>V = V ? V + DayOfMonth.V : DayOfMonth.V;</tag><ruleref uri='date.grxml#MonthOfYear'/><tag>V = V ? V + MonthOfYear.V : MonthOfYear.V;</tag><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomRegexEntity\nreason: The GRXML grammar provided involves matching a driver's license format consisting of combinations of names, digits, specific numeric sequences, and date elements. This does not match any of the provided built-in entity types, as it represents a specific structured input rather than a predefined entity (e.g., Age, Date, Phone number). It also isn't a suitable ClosedListEntity, given the open-ended structured responses. Hence, a RegexEntity should be used to validate the provided format using regular expressions.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_QC\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_QC\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '^([A-Za-z]{1,})(\\d{1,})(999999|\\d{2}\\d{2}\\d{2})(\\d{2})$'\n      validationMessage: 'Please enter a valid driver license number (e.g., Name followed by digits and date format or 999999).'"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert the file DL_QC to Microsoft Copilot Studio Yaml.  File content:      <grammar version='1.0' xml:lang='es-us' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2001/06/grammar' root='_ROOT_'><rule id='_ROOT_' scope='public'><one-of><item><ruleref uri='#license'/><tag>if (SWI_vars.disallow) { var disallow_arr = SWI_vars.disallow.split('^'); disallowList = SWI_vars.disallow; for (var i=0; i &lt; disallow_arr.length; i++) { if (license.SWI_meaning == disallow_arr[i]) { SWI_disallow=1; break; } } } if(license.SWI_meaning) {SWI_meaning=license.SWI_meaning; dm_root=license.SWI_meaning;}; if(license.dm_command) {SWI_meaning=license.dm_command; dm_command=license.dm_command}; if(license.dm_confirmation_mode) {dm_confirmation_mode=license.dm_confirmation_mode}; if(license.dm_confirm_string) {dm_confirm_string=license.dm_confirm_string}; grammar_version='20180502'; MEANING=SWI_meaning; if (SWI_meaning.substring(4,5) === '0'){SWI_disallow=1;} ps_gramlib_id='untested_nr10_esus_drivers_license_QC';</tag></item></one-of></rule><rule id='license' scope='public'><ruleref uri='soundexLastName.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + S.V : S.V;</tag><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag><one-of><item>nueve nueve nueve nueve nueve nueve<tag>V = V ? V + '999999' : '999999';</tag></item><item><ruleref uri='date.grxml#DayOfMonth'/><tag>V = V ? V + DayOfMonth.V : DayOfMonth.V;</tag><ruleref uri='date.grxml#MonthOfYear'/><tag>V = V ? V + MonthOfYear.V : MonthOfYear.V;</tag><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item></item></one-of><item repeat='2'><ruleref uri='digit.grxml'/><tag>V = V ? V + D.V : D.V;</tag></item><tag>SWI_meaning=V;</tag></rule></grammar>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "entity_type: CustomEntity (RegexEntity)\nreason: The provided GRXML grammar defines a structured pattern involving soundexLastName (alphanumeric), digits, specific number sequences (\"999999\"), dates (day/month), and additional digits. Such a specific combination can be best represented through regular expressions (RegexEntity) in Copilot Studio. It is neither a simple predefined nor entirely a closed list entity.\ncopilot_studio_code: |\n  - kind: CustomEntityComponent\n    displayName: DL_QC\n    state: Active\n    status: Active\n    schemaName: DL_QC\n    entity:\n      kind: RegexEntity\n      regexPattern: '[A-Za-z]+\\d+(999999|(\\d{2}\\d{2}\\d{2}))\\d{2}'\n      validationMessage: \"Please enter a valid driver's license format according to the pattern.\"\n\n# Explanation of regex:\n# [A-Za-z]+ matches the license holder's last name (soundex representation assumed).\n# \\d+ matches the numbers following the last name.\n# (999999|(\\d{2}\\d{2}\\d{2})) covers either '999999' specifically, or a combination of two-digit day, month, and two-digit year.\n# \\d{2} at the end accounts for the additional two digits required. \n\nNote: You may need to slightly adapt the regex depending on detailed soundex rules and digit sequences used in the legacy GRXML implementation."}]}
